      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "$\\boxed{4}$. To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm is based on the principle that the GCD of two numbers also divides their difference.\n\nHere are the steps to find the GCD of 12 and 20 using the Euclidean algorithm:\n\n1. Divide 20 by 12 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   20 = 12 \\times 1 + 8\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is 8.\n\n2. Now, divide 12 by 8 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   12 = 8 \\times 1 + 4\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is 4.\n\n3. Finally, divide 8 by 4 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   8 = 4 \\times 2 + 0\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is 0.\n\nSince the remainder is now 0, the GCD of 12 and 20 is the last non-zero remainder, which is 4.\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\boxed{4}.",
